# Getting Started with Oriel

## Installation

Install the Oriel CLI:

```sh
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/highercomve/Oriel/main/install.sh | sh
```

## Verify Your System

Check that your system has all required dependencies:

```sh
oriel doctor
```

Oriel requires:
- Zig 0.16.0
- GTK 4 and WebKitGTK 6.0 (development packages)
- Node.js (for Vite frontends)

## Create Your First App

Create a new Oriel project:

```sh
oriel init my-app
cd my-app
```

Choose a template:
- React + Vite (default)
- Vue + Vite
- Svelte + Vite
- Vanilla JavaScript + Vite

## Start Development

```sh
oriel dev
```

This starts the Vite dev server and launches your app with hot reload.

## Build for Release

```sh
oriel build
```

Then package it:

```sh
oriel package
```

This creates deb, rpm, and AppImage packages for Linux.

## Next Steps

- Read the tutorial to build a complete example app
- Explore the modules for tray, SQLite, updater, and more
- Check the GitHub repository for examples
